WEBVTT

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:10.820
Inuzuka-san, you're good at painting those lines!

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.690
Am I?

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.600
Well, you know. He's a teacher.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.370
Does that make a difference?

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.000
Maybe not, I guess.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.950
Fathers!

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.440
The kids are cutting vegetables.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.420
If you'd like to watch, come on in.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.060
They're cutting vegetables?

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.330
Really?

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.200
They're using children's knives.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.220
It should be fine.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.220
<b>Summer Break Sleepover</b>

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.220
Okay, it's time for a summer break special!

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.520
Our dinner for the sleepover will be curry!

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.600
Let's all work together and make it taste great!

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.750
Okay!

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.950
We'll do this in order.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.280
First, Tsumugi-chan.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.070
Okay!

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.810
Hold the knife tight, Tsumugi-chan.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:03.540
'Kay!

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.260
Fingers in, like a kitty paw.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.460
Meow!

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.470
Well done!

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.410
Did you see me, Daddy?

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.640
I did! That was great, Tsumugi!

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.080
Bye-bye!

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.400
Oh, my... Yeah.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.340
Children's knives, huh?

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.820
The curry we all made together is done!

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.770
Now, put your hands together and...

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.510
Let's eat!

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.590
Let's eat!

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:57.000
It's so yum!

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.050
It's "delicious," you mean!

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:00.510
Yum!

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.170
Yum!

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.470
Yum!

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:07.810
It's delicious!

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.310
It's delicious, huh?

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.100
Yup!

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.810
Is this the carrot I cut?

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.240
It might be mine.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.270
At-home curry is good,

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.760
but this is close to it, and it's good, too!

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.620
This is regular curry.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.210
The kind you get at a restaurant.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.480
At-home curry is different!

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.040
It's got grapes and stuff!

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.180
Grapes?

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.890
Does she mean raisins?

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.590
Yeah, that! Probably!

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:45.640
And...

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.600
It was really good.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.480
That's right.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.470
The curry we had at home was more...

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.500
<b>Our Family's At-Home Curry</b>

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:43.180
Stay within the white lines 
when your sparkler's lit.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:46.140
Don't bump into your friends.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.400
Daddy, look!

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.780
It's so pretty!

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:52.470
Yeah.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.560
It's so cute!

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.900
It sure is!

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.570
Wow, my sparkler's awesome!

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.130
Mine's more awesome!

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:04.450
What?!

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.070
Mine's more awesome!

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.420
Stay in the circle!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.960
Let me go!

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.000
No!

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:17.640
You'll all be staying here tonight.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:20.710
Say goodnight to your families, okay?

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.220
Goodnight!

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.220
Goodnight!

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.760
We'll come to get you tomorrow!

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.070
'Kay!

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:33.100
Night, Daddy!

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:35.140
Night!

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.340
Is he gonna be okay?

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.680
I wonder if she'll cry...

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:42.920
Really?

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.770
What?

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.410
I'm home.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:14.100
Maybe I'll wash the dishes from this morning.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.230
Is Tsumugi asleep like she should be?

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.400
I wanna go home!

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.500
I wanna go home!

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.510
Mikio-kun, let's get you into your futon.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.930
I'll pat you on your back to help you sleep.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.990
I wanna go home!

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:09.990
It's okay, it's okay.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:19.290
Hello?

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.340
<i>Yo. Today was the sleepover, right?</i>

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:25.880
Yeah. I just got home.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.280
Did you eat?

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.220
<i>The kids made curry at the school.</i>

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.850
<i>We ate it together.</i>

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:33.470
I see.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.890
So what are you going to do? 
Want to come get a drink?

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:41.240
Nah, I want to be able to drive if I have to.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.150
Sorry, but I'll pass today.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:45.050
I see.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:48.110
Don't cry with Tsumugi gone.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.340
Oh, right.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:56.920
What do you call curry with little 
pieces of meat and raisins, again?

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:57.830
<i>Huh?</i>

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.870
You mean ground beef?

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.500
<i>It's not a liquid curry.</i>

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.790
Keema, or dry curry.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.210
That might be it!

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.000
Thanks! Bye!

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:27.300
Okay!

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:47.920
It's from Sensei!

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.740
What could it be?

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:56.390
Dry curry?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:58.890
I'm home!

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.150
I'm home!

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.470
I'm home!

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:03.910
I'm home!

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.960
I'm home, Mr. Galigali!

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:11.860
I had a sleepover at school last night!

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:15.320
Tsumugi, wash your hands and gargle.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:16.550
Okay!

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:25.370
New Message
From: Iida Kotori (1-A)
Re: 

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:21.130
<i>Hello.</i>

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:23.500
<i>I like dry curry, too!</i>

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.370
<i>I like all curry!</i>

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.840
<i>So, question for you!</i>

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:34.800
<b>So, question for you!
If you know what kinds of toppings
or curry roux or spices you used, 
please tell me.</b>

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:34.800
<i>if you know what kinds of toppings or curry 
roux or spices you used, please tell me.</i>

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.800
Ingredients... Ingredients, huh?

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:42.210
Did we have any roux or spices left?

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:43.810
I think we kept them here...

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:48.250
This is...

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:56.650
<b>Ginger Pork</b>

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:51.880
The recipe notebook!

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.160
So that's where it was.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.100
I never found it because I only 
checked the bookshelves!

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:58.740
Huh?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.690
Th-There are only three pages?

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.980
But that's just like her...

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.300
Let's see... Yellowtail with daikon...

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.720
There's a recipe for dry curry!

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.670
I washed my hands! What's that?

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:19.050
Tsumugi, let's make at-home curry next!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.050
At-home curry?!

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:25.390
You mean... <i>that</i> curry with... <i>that</i>?

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.590
That's right.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:29.710
Our family's at-home curry, with the raisins in it.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.960
Hooray!

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:34.860
All right, I'll fax this over...

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.490
No, wait. I should copy it first...

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:40.720
At-home curry! At-home curry!

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:44.040
Mr. Galigali, Mommy's at-home curry

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.500
is a magically sweet curry!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.300
Whoa... What is it?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:11.200
When do we eat it?

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:12.430
Tomorrow?

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:14.570
Tomorrow may be too soon.

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:25.780
Since we have your family's recipe today,

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:28.190
we won't change it to 
make it easier for beginners.

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:30.870
My mom just rewrote it 
to be easier to understand.

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:32.360
Okay!

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:34.540
Here are the ingredients we'll use.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:39.080
I-I didn't realize it had this much in it.

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:41.050
Treasures!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:44.600
It looks like she used whatever 
vegetables were in season.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:50.110
Oh, and it's easier if you measure out 
the curry powder and spices first,

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:51.980
so I've done that.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:54.510
The first step is to cut the vegetables—

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:55.030
'Kay!

00:11:55.510 --> 00:11:56.440
'Kay?

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.920
I can use a knife!

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:03.610
We don't have a children's knife today,

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.610
so there's no cutting for you to do.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:08.320
Why not?! Why not?!

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:10.040
I can use a knife!

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.290
It's dangerous!

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:21.070
You only get to use the grown-up 
knife when Daddy's with you.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:22.120
Got it?

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:22.720
Yup!

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:31.070
What do you do with the hand 
holding the vegetable?

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:31.880
Meow!

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:35.310
Chop, chop, chop, and we're done, okay?

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:35.990
Okay...

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.220
I worked hard, so I'm done.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.120
Right.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:05.940
Thank you for helping.

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.700
This could be trouble.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:13.650
She learned how to use a children's knife 
at the kindergarten sleepover,

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.820
so she wanted to try again.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:17.600
I see.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.510
Do these all get minced?

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:21.970
Oh, yes.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:25.290
All right! Leave the mincing to me!

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:27.070
It's all yours.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:32.730
Ts-Tsumugi-chan used a knife...

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:36.040
And I still can't even...

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:41.530
The onions are stinging my eyes...

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:42.920
You can do it!

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:47.480
All right, now we fry the ingredients.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:52.750
Make 300 milliliters of soup 
with some boullion, okay?

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:53.480
Okay.

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:59.480
First, fry the garlic and ginger.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.040
Once you can smell them,

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:04.570
add the onions.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.580
Once the onions turn clear,

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.260
add the carrots, celery, and eggplant...

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.020
Then fry.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.240
Add the ground beef,

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:16.620
and once it's browned,

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:20.630
we add curry powder and salt.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.700
Now we just add in the other things 
we've cut and stew them.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:28.620
If you can do the mincing,
the rest is surprisingly easy, huh?

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:29.630
It is.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.080
Now add the tomatoes, and wait for it to boil.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:38.770
Once it boils, add in the grated apple, 
raisins, green peppers, and soup.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:40.650
Um...

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.830
Apples, raisins,

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:44.610
green peppers...

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:46.610
Green peppers?

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:49.420
She couldn't eat green peppers even when

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:51.530
we put them in gratin, 
one of her favorite meals.

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:55.660
Tsumugi-chan's eaten all kinds of things,

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:59.990
but green peppers were the 
one thing she couldn't handle...

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:09.790
Ts-Tsumugi-chan, there are 
green peppers in the curry.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:10.590
I know!

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:14.090
Is it okay to put them in?

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:15.590
It's okay!

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:16.970
It is?

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:19.340
Sweet at-home curry

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:22.810
uses magic to make any vegetable curry-flavored!

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:24.520
Magic?

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.000
I know that curry's delicious!

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.510
I... I see!

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.570
That's amazing magic, huh?

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:38.200
Now we let it sit for ten minutes 
on medium-high heat.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.500
That's how we get the moisture 
to bubble out so it dries.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:45.020
Bubble bubble bubble! Bubble bubble bubble!

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.730
Bubble! Bubble! Bubble! Bubble!

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:48.250
Bubble! Bubble! Bubble!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.600
Okay, it's been ten minutes.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:54.860
We'll remove Tsumugi's portion now.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.820
Before we put this in?

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:58.670
Yes.

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:03.730
You can adjust the spiciness of 
this dry curry for adults and kids.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:09.280
When you put in the garam masala,
it becomes spicy.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.330
So if you take out the kids' 
share before you put it in,

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:15.980
you don't have to make separate 
dishes for the adults and the kids.

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:17.680
I see!

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:20.750
It feels like you're eating the same curry, right?

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:27.040
My mom said your wife must've 
been a really good mother.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.170
Yeah.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.760
Thank you.

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:35.000
It smells so good!

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:38.290
It really does.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:39.980
It makes you hungry, right?

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:41.640
Yeah! Super hungry!

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.980
All right, let's make the rest!

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:50.690
Okay. We'll taste the grown-up curry,
and if there's not enough salt, we'll add more.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.490
You add the garam masala 
just before you turn off the heat,

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.670
to make it as spicy as you want it.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:05.210
Okay!

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:09.170
It's done!

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:16.180
The Inuzuka family's at-home curry!

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:19.460
Wow! Wow!

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:22.160
I made the rice a little firmer than usual

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:23.630
and mixed in some brown rice.

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:25.140
Looks yummy!

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:27.150
Let's eat! Let's eat!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.420
Let's eat!

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:44.540
I wasn't sure how curry with raisins would taste,

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:47.110
but this is really good!

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:50.790
Isn't at-home curry good?

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:53.760
Yeah! It is!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:57.430
Your family's at-home curry is so good!

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.340
Ts-Tsumugi!

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:09.420
Calm down! Chew your food slowly!

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:11.060
Don't worry.

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:15.280
I got her an extra portion.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:18.490
I can't stop!

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:22.320
Well, I guess you can't help it.

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:24.650
At-home curry is that good, huh?

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:26.410
Yeah! I can't help it!

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.340
What's for dinner today?

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:55.150
What's wrong?

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.600
Seconds!

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:33.200
You really like at-home curry, 
huh, Tsumugi-chan?

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.370
I sure do!

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:39.900
Thank you.

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:41.340
No, thank you.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:44.930
Tsumugi-chan, goodnight.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:46.280
Goodnight!

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.910
What're you laughing at?

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:58.250
Oh, I just remembered something...

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:03.720
That time when Mommy was crying 
because she'd been mincing onions,

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.160
she was making curry, right?

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:10.730
That was when she put on 
your glasses and got dizzy!

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:12.190
Yeah, that's right!

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:14.460
Me, too!

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:17.150
I remembered that earlier, too!

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.470
That was when she made a funny face, right?

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:21.840
Huh? Did she really?

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.100
Really! Really!

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:24.250
We both remembered!

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:26.000
I see.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.510
So we both remembered, huh?

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:37.050
Tsumugi? What's wrong?

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:43.160
Tsumugi?

00:20:44.690 --> 00:20:47.140
Mommy's not coming...

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:54.520
Daddy makes it instead...

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:08.390
I'm sorry.

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:09.850
I'm sorry...

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.960
I won't make it any—

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:23.560
I'll eat it!

00:21:38.180 --> 00:21:40.820
At-home curry was good,

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:43.000
wasn't it, Tsumugi?

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:44.990
Yeah.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:47.590
It was good.
